# Script B of the two-library gate (two-library-gate.md, section 5), as the engine's gate test runs it.
# The lines a script has (script-a.steps uses all but carries and driver; the programs' scenarios use carries):
#   load FILE                          the text loaded, beside this file
#   stand-in: EFFECT(F, ...) -> ANSWER  an answer of the stand-in driver, used once, by the first Effect that fits
#                                      (`_` fits any field); ANSWER is a value, then `; DIM N` for each cost and
#                                      `; EVENT(...)` for each Event performed with it; an Effect met with no answer
#                                      left fails the step, by name
#   carries: EFFECT, ...               Effects the stand-in carries beyond those its answers name (it answers them
#                                      only from stand-in lines)
#   driver: EVENT(...) -> RESULT       the stand-in performs EVENT on its own; RESULT is performed or refused ...
#   PARTY: ACT -> RESULT -> ...        PARTY asks for ACT; the RESULTs are all of its results, in order: performed,
#                                      refused source, refused policy, refused closes, ended VALUE, raised EFFECT
#   holds FACT | not FACT              what holds afterwards
#   violated DUTY | unviolated DUTY    whether a duty is violated
#   record has TEXT | record lacks TEXT  whether a line the last step wrote holds TEXT, as the engine writes it
#                                      without quotes
# A word alone is a text, `"..."` a text with any sign in it, digits a number, true and false a truth, `[a, b]` a
# list, `Name { f: a, g: b }` a record, `Name(...)` a constructor, `{ ... }` a filling's text.
load library-b.docket
p1: Write(p1, m1, t1) -> performed -> ended ()
p1: Cross(p1, m1, t2) -> performed -> ended ()
holds On(m1, t1)
holds On(m1, t2)
p1: Share(p1, m1, p2) -> performed -> ended ()
holds Owner(m1, p1)
holds Owner(m1, p2)
p1: Star-It(p1, m1) -> performed -> ended ()
p2: Star-It(p2, m1) -> performed -> ended ()
p3: Star-It(p3, m1) -> performed -> ended ()
holds Stars(m1, 3)
p3: Cross(p3, m1, t3) -> refused policy -> raised Refused
p2: Write(p2, m2, t1) -> performed -> ended ()
p2: Put-After(p2, t1, m2, m1) -> performed -> ended ()
holds After(t1, m2, m1)
p1: Archive(p1, t2) -> performed -> ended ()
holds Archived(t2)
p2: Cross(p2, m2, t2) -> refused policy -> raised Refused
p1: Yield(p1, m1) -> performed -> ended ()
not Owner(m1, p1)
p2: Yield(p2, m1) -> refused policy -> raised Refused
holds Owner(m1, p2)
